    "title": "Man charged in Harrisburg stabbing death of woman - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Kaylee Lindenmuth ,\n2 hours ago HARRISBURG, Pa. (WHTM) — A man is facing a murder charge after police alleged he stabbed a woman, killing her, before stabbing himself.\nRocheny Clerge, 33, is facing charges of murder and possession of an instrument of crime, according to Harrisburg Police.\nHe is accused in the stabbing death of 31-year-old Violette Pierre last Tuesday on the 300 block of South 17th Street.\nPierre was found dead at the scene with Clerge nearby, injured, police said. He was taken to an area hospital for treatment of his injuries.\nPolice said, through investigation, they believed Clerge was responsible for Pierre’s death.\nThe investigation remains ongoing and anyone with information is asked to call Harrisburg Police at 717-558-6900.\nCopyright 2025 Nexstar Media, Inc. All rights reserved. This material may not be published, broadcast, rewritten, or redistributed. For the latest news, weather, sports, and streaming video, head to ABC27.\n1",
